{%- comment -%}
  Brand story — a narrative trust beat in place of a review-widget block:
  builds trust through the store's own voice instead of borrowed star
  ratings.

  Layout: 50/50 split — copy on one side, one full-bleed portrait 3:4
  photograph on the other, running to the page edge. Below 900px it stacks
  image first, copy under it. With no image the section is one column of copy
  (see NO PLACEHOLDER below).

  COPY RULES (hard, not stylistic):
    · No craftsmanship, atelier, workshop or artisan claims unless the brand
      can back them.
    · No heritage, founding-year or "generations" story unless it's true.
    · No natural-fibre claims unless the material is verified — treat as
      imitation/blend otherwise.
    · No model measurements when the models are AI-generated.
    · No "small shop run by one person" framing: the shopper is buying
      clothes, not a founder story. The voice is about curation and
      effortless dressing, not about who packs the boxes.
  Everything the default copy asserts should be verifiable: a deliberately
  small edit, honest photography, published sizing, email answered by a
  person. The shipped text is a PROPOSAL and every line is a section
  setting.

  Image: ONE portrait 3:4 editorial photograph — its own atmosphere frame (no
  model), kept distinct from the homepage imagery so the PDP never repeats a
  picture.

  NO PLACEHOLDER HERE. This slot used to fall back to Shopify's
  `lifestyle-2` placeholder_svg_tag, which is a stock line drawing of cameras,
  watches and a compass. On a fashion label that single graphic disqualifies the
  store on sight — it says "demo data" louder than any copy on the page can say
  otherwise, and it is the illustration a shopper meets in the first second of
  scrolling. An unset image now renders NOTHING: the section drops to one column
  (data-media="none") and reads as a deliberate type-only statement, which is a
  defensible look. A clip-art camera is not.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign story_url = section.settings.link
  if story_url == blank and section.settings.page != blank
    assign story_url = section.settings.page.url
  endif

  comment
    Three ways to name the photograph, resolved to one. Priority is
    asset filename → product's featured image → image_picker, unchanged from
    before so no live store loses its picture; the picker is the documented
    slot and the other two stay as the escape hatches they already were.
  endcomment
  assign bs_img = section.settings.image
  if section.settings.image_product != blank and section.settings.image_product.featured_image != blank
    assign bs_img = section.settings.image_product.featured_image
  endif
  assign bs_asset = section.settings.asset_image
  assign bs_has_media = false
  if bs_asset != blank or bs_img != blank
    assign bs_has_media = true
  endif
-%}
<section
  class="story bleed reveal"
  data-media="{% if bs_has_media %}image{% else %}none{% endif %}"
  aria-label="{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}"
>
  {%- if bs_has_media -%}
    <div class="story__art">
      {%- if bs_asset != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%} A theme asset has no Shopify image object, so there is no
        real width/height to declare — 1200×1600 is the documented 3:4 target and
        holds the box against layout shift even if the file shipped is off-ratio
        (object-fit crops it to 3:4 either way). {%- endcomment -%}
        <img src="{{ bs_asset | asset_url }}" sizes="(max-width: 899px) 100vw, 50vw" width="1200" height="1600" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      {%- else -%}
        <img
          src="{{ bs_img | image_url: width: 900 }}"
          srcset="{{ bs_img | image_url: width: 560 }} 560w, {{ bs_img | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w, {{ bs_img | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w"
          sizes="(max-width: 899px) 100vw, 50vw"
          width="{{ bs_img.width }}" height="{{ bs_img.height }}"
          alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- liquid
    comment
      Every field the merchant filled in wins, in every language — Translate &
      Adapt localizes section settings, so a secondary locale already holds the
      translated copy. The locale file only fills a field left blank. The old
      version reassigned all four on any non-primary locale, which replaced a
      merchant's own brand story with the theme's default copy — the worst place
      for it, since this section is explicitly the store's own voice.

      Eyebrow and link_label keep blank-means-hidden (each has an != blank guard
      below), so only the two structural fields fall back.
    endcomment
    assign st_eyebrow = section.settings.eyebrow
    assign st_link = section.settings.link_label
    assign st_heading = section.settings.heading
    if st_heading == blank
      assign st_heading = 'pdp_story.heading' | t
    endif
    assign st_text = section.settings.text
    if st_text == blank
      assign st_text = 'pdp_story.text_html' | t
    endif
  -%}
  <div class="story__body">
    {%- if st_eyebrow != blank -%}
      <p class="lbl-sm mute">{{ st_eyebrow | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if st_heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="dm">{{ st_heading | escape }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if st_text != blank -%}
      <div class="prose story__text">{{ st_text }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if st_link != blank and story_url != blank -%}
      <a class="tlink" href="{{ story_url }}">{{ st_link | escape }}</a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Brand story",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Trust through the store's own voice. Never claim craftsmanship, an atelier, a heritage or a natural fibre here unless the brand can back it — unsubstantiated claims risk a Google Merchant Center misrepresentation flag." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image", "info": "Portrait 3:4, 1200 × 1600. Runs full-bleed on one half. Leave empty and the section renders as copy only — no placeholder graphic." },
    { "type": "product", "id": "image_product", "label": "Or: product whose model photo to show", "info": "Uses the product's featured image (can crop awkwardly — prefer the asset filename below)." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "asset_image", "label": "Or: theme-asset filename (wins over both)", "info": "e.g. my-image.webp — dedicated portrait 3:4 shot." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Our approach" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Effortless, on purpose" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "<p>This is an edit, not a catalogue. A piece earns its place when it goes on without thinking and still looks considered at the end of a long day: colours that live happily next to each other, shapes that layer, nothing that waits for an occasion.</p><p>We would rather carry fewer things and stand behind each one: honest photography, sizing you can check before you buy, and prices we can explain. If something is not right, you write to us and a person writes back.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "link_label", "label": "Link label", "default": "About us" },
    { "type": "page", "id": "page", "label": "Link page" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link", "label": "Link override", "info": "Leave empty to link to the page above." }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Brand story",
      "settings": {
        "image": "",
        "eyebrow": "Our approach",
        "heading": "Effortless, on purpose",
        "link_label": "About us"
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
